{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And she could no longer hide him.</b> Rashi's interpretation: she gave birth to him at six months and one day, and they searched for him at the end of nine. And if you ask: but we say in Sotah that she had been pregnant with him three months before she took him back. One may answer: they searched for him at the end of three months from when she took him back, which are nine months from when she conceived from him, for they knew that she who gives birth at seven gives birth at partial months, and he was born at the end of three months from the return — therefore she could no longer hide him except three months." "<b>The word גמא.</b> Because it resembles סוף, in which he was cast." "<b>ותחמרה.</b> The heh is weak (without dagesh)." "<b>In clay.</b> On the inside, <b>and in pitch</b> on the outside. For had the clay been on the outside, the water would have dissolved it. <b>And she placed it among the reeds</b> — so that the ark would not be seen there, because גומא and סוף are one species, and her intention was to steal him away from there, but Pharaoh's daughter preceded her." "<b>On the bank of the river.</b> She could not put it in the river completely surrounded on all sides, but only from the bank side of the river, and therefore Pharaoh's daughter saw it, for she was bathing inside the river; but her maidens who walked along the bank of the river could not see it."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {2 "Chizkuni notes the unaspirated heh at the end of ותחמרה, indicating it is a weak (raphe) letter rather than carrying a dagesh."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:55:49.897600884Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}